    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSR575/product-development-engineer-materials-and-data-ktp-associate-sbd-apparel": {
      "title": "Product Development Engineer (Materials & Data) (KTP Associate @ SBD Apparel)",
      "description": "Product Development Engineer (Materials & Data) (KTP Associate @ SBD Apparel) at Sheffield Hallam University This site uses cookies to store information on your computer. Some of these cookies are essential, while others help us to improve your experience by providing insights into how the site is being used. For more detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our Cookie policy I Accept Cookies I Do Not Accept Cookies Necessary Cookies Necessary cookies enable core functionality such as page navigation and access to secure areas. The website cannot function properly without these cookies, and can only be disabled by changing your browser preferences. Functional Cookies These help us to personalise the website to you by remembering your preferences and settings. functional On Off Marketing Cookies Marketing cookies help us provide personalised and relevant services or advertising to our website visitors, and to assess the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns. marketing On Off Analytics Cookies Analytical cookies help us to improve our website by collecting and reporting information on its usage. analytics On Off About this tool (Opens in a new window) Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to \n            search results Product Development Engineer (Materials & Data) (KTP Associate @ SBD Apparel) Sheffield Hallam University - School of Sport and Physical Activity Location: Sheffield Salary: £32,080 to £40,000\n                                                                                        per annum, depending on experience. Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Fixed-Term/Contract Placed On: 21st August 2026 Closes: 9th September 2026 Job Ref: 119567 Fixed term (24 months) Full time – 37 hours per week Closing date : 09/09/2026 at 23:30 The Role This role offers an exciting opportunity to lead a high-impact, industry-focused project to inform product design based on the intersection of sports engineering and materials science with a market-leading, global company. You will work closely with both Sheffield Hallam University and SBD Apparel, developing and implementing data-driven testing methodologies to inform material selection and product development. It will appeal to individuals passionate about applying research in a real-world manufacturing environment, offering the chance to directly innovate and influence the next-generation of strength sport apparel while gaining valuable experience across academia and industry. The Company Partner SBD is a global sportswear brand, designing and manufacturing market-leading performance products for strength sports. Our team is proud to craft all our products in the United Kingdom, with the majority fully manufactured at our headquarters on the Advanced Manufacturing Park, Rotherham. Our commitment to quality has seen our products become the standard among strength athletes in gyms across the world, including those competing in the World’s Strongest Man, the IPF World Powerlifting Championships, and the IWF World Weightlifting Championships. The Project The project will support SBD’s continued innovation by developing an advanced, data-driven framework for the testing, evaluation and selection of materials used in strength-sport technical clothing and supports. The project will investigate how material properties influence performance, durability and comfort across different training and competition contexts. By integrating experimental testing, data analysis, and product design considerations, the project will enable more informed, evidence-based materials choices and support the development of the next-generation strength sport products. You will work closely with SBD’s product development and manufacturing teams, embedding new testing methodologies and technical knowledge within the company, strengthening SBD’s capability to innovate and deliver performance-led products at all competition levels. Benefits Sheffield Hallam offers a wide range of benefits and opportunities to pursue a rewarding and fulfilling career in a supportive environment. This appointment also carries a range of benefits including: A generous training and personal development budget, with allocated time to further develop your technical skills. Off-site KTP management training Gaining experience in managing and delivering a high-profile project for a global sports apparel company. The opportunity to register for a higher degree for which tuition fees will be waived (if applicable) Complimentary breakfast and lunch when working onsite at SBD headquarters 40% Staff discount on SBD products Complimentary strength sports events tickets Although the appointment duration is 24 months, it is possible that a permanent position may be available within the company upon successful completion of the project where you can take a leading role in technical development. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from Sheffield Hallam University Lecturer in Chemistry Associate Lecturer in Child Nursing Academic Tutors – 2 roles Researcher - Sustainable Futures and Supply Chain Academic Tutor in Cyber Security Academic Tutor in Computer Science and Software Engineering Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Re