    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSN000/academic-tutor-aerospace-engineering": {
      "title": "This site uses cookies to store information on your computer.",
      "description": "Academic Tutor – Aerospace Engineering at Sheffield Hallam University This site uses cookies to store information on your computer. Some of these cookies are essential, while others help us to improve your experience by providing insights into how the site is being used. For more detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our Cookie policy I Accept Cookies I Do Not Accept Cookies Necessary Cookies Necessary cookies enable core functionality such as page navigation and access to secure areas. The website cannot function properly without these cookies, and can only be disabled by changing your browser preferences. Functional Cookies These help us to personalise the website to you by remembering your preferences and settings. functional On Off Marketing Cookies Marketing cookies help us provide personalised and relevant services or advertising to our website visitors, and to assess the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns. marketing On Off Analytics Cookies Analytical cookies help us to improve our website by collecting and reporting information on its usage. analytics On Off About this tool (Opens in a new window) Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to \n            search results Academic Tutor – Aerospace Engineering Sheffield Hallam University - College of Business, Technology and Engineering / School of Engineering and Built Environment Location: Sheffield Salary: £32,080 to £38,784 Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 5th August 2026 Closes: 6th September 2026 Job Ref: 119107 We are looking to appoint an Academic Tutor in Aerospace Engineering to help inspire the next generation of engineers tackling the challenges of air, space and sustainable transportation. The successful candidate will have a broad background in aerospace engineering, with the ability to support students in applying engineering principles, design, analysis and systems thinking to real-world challenges. Experience gained through academic study, industrial practice or other professional activity, and applicable across aerospace, automotive or railway engineering, would be welcomed. Working within the Future Transportation Subject Area, you will contribute to a professional-from-day-one, project-based curriculum through a range of teaching, learning and assessment activities, while supporting module development and curriculum enhancement. The role will primarily support Aerospace Engineering, while also contributing across Automotive Engineering and Railway Engineering in line with teaching and curriculum needs The School of Engineering and Built Environment brings together engineering, construction and surveying, physics and the built environment. With excellent links to industry, we provide applied learning opportunities for students and our graduates perform strongly in the labour market. Emphasis is also placed on Research, Innovation and Knowledge Exchange within the School and there is firm alignment with UKRI priority areas. We are a welcoming community where staff and students are encouraged to develop their careers and make a fulfilling impact. We offer a diverse range of benefits and opportunities to pursue a rewarding and fulfilling career in a supportive environment. The University currently enrols eligible academic staff into the Teachers’ Pension Scheme (TPS), a defined-benefit pension scheme. Should you be enrolled into TPS, each year you will earn a secure pension benefit of 1/57th of your salary and the University will pay pension contributions towards the cost of this pension (currently worth about 29% of your salary). For a salary of £35,000, for example, the University would pay just over £10,000 in the first year of your employment and you would earn a pension of £614 p.a. for that year (payable from your State Pension Age). Further details on TPS can be found here If you’re a member of the Universities Superannuation Scheme (USS) directly before joining us, you can choose to remain in USS instead. We welcome applications for job-share, part-time and flexible working arrangements. To find out more, take a look at our guide to applying . We recommend you download the job description and person specification when you apply, as this will not be available once the job has closed. Accessibility We are committed to ensuring our materials are accessible to all. If you encounter any accessibility barriers or have suggestions for improvement please contact us using our web accessibility report form . Your feedback helps us enhance our accessibility efforts and improve our services. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from Sheffield Hallam University Lecturer in Chemistry Associate Lecturer in Child Nursing Academic Tutors – 2 roles Researcher - Sustainable Futures and Supply Chain Product Development Engineer (Materials & Data) (KTP Associate @ SBD Apparel) Academic Tutor in Cyber Security Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Lecturer in Renewable Energy and Life Cycle Sustainability Research Associate/Senior Research Associate in Control for Soft Robot Wearable Assistance Professor in Aerospace and Future Flight Reader in Aerospace Stipendiary and Non-Stipendiary Research Fellowships Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
