    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSR522/academic-tutors-2-roles": {
      "title": "This site uses cookies to store information on your computer.",
      "description": "Academic Tutors – 2 roles at Sheffield Hallam University This site uses cookies to store information on your computer. Some of these cookies are essential, while others help us to improve your experience by providing insights into how the site is being used. For more detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our Cookie policy I Accept Cookies I Do Not Accept Cookies Necessary Cookies Necessary cookies enable core functionality such as page navigation and access to secure areas. The website cannot function properly without these cookies, and can only be disabled by changing your browser preferences. Functional Cookies These help us to personalise the website to you by remembering your preferences and settings. functional On Off Marketing Cookies Marketing cookies help us provide personalised and relevant services or advertising to our website visitors, and to assess the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns. marketing On Off Analytics Cookies Analytical cookies help us to improve our website by collecting and reporting information on its usage. analytics On Off About this tool (Opens in a new window) Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to \n            search results Academic Tutors – 2 roles Sheffield Hallam University - Robotics Engineering or Electrical/Electronic Engineering Location: Sheffield Salary: £32,080 to £38,784\n                                                                                        per annum, depending on experience Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 21st August 2026 Closes: 9th September 2026 Job Ref: 118889 Permanent Full time – 37 hours per week Closing date 09/09/2026 at 23:30 The Role We are recruiting for 2 x Academic Tutors to join our existing team and welcome applications from candidates with practical experience in: Power Systems & Machines Analogue & Digital Electronics Control & Automation Robotics As part of your role you will be delivering labs, supporting other academic colleagues in their teaching and leading on outreach and recruitment events. You will also be supporting   students on their employability journey by supervising placements and engaging with our industry partners to enhance our academic delivery offer.  These are brand new roles to our team and therefore you can really make an impact on how the role is delivered.   We are looking for people with a passion for Engineering to engage our students and provide excellent student experiences. You will be supported by the wider academic team in your role. Applicants should have an awareness of the current trends, issues, and developments in electrical/electronic engineering both nationally and internationally, and will be expected to demonstrate an applied understanding of current industry developments during the selection process. You do not need previous experience of teaching, as this is a great opportunity for an applicant with practical industry experience  or if you are a professional already teaching in an FE environment  with a desire to inspire the next generation of Electrica/Electronic/Mechatronic Engineers. The subject group also leads the MSc Electrical & Electronic Engineering course and teaches extensively across the MSc Engineering portfolio as well as the Degree Apprenticeship Programs. We also make a significant contribution to other engineering BEng and MSc programmes in the department and the delivery of degree apprenticeship courses across the University. The Team You will be a key member of the Electrical Electronic and Future Technologies team, helping to maintain and to expand the success of the department's courses in this area. Our courses are highly regarded across the profession and founded upon over 30 years of related teaching here at SHU. Our courses are accredited by the relevant professional bodies, and staff members are encouraged to be active within them. Courses within our departmental portfolio are accredited by the following UK professional bodies: IET The School of Engineering and Built Environment is arranged into a number of subject areas: Electrical, Electronic and Future Technologies, Mechanical Engineering, Future Transportation, Built Environment, and Energy, Infrastructure and Environment.  We place equal emphasis on teaching and research, be it subject or pedagogic research into teaching Engineering, Physics and Built Environment to transform lives. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from Sheffield Hallam University Lecturer in Chemistry Associate Lecturer in Child Nursing Researcher - Sustainable Futures and Supply Chain Product Development Engineer (Materials & Data) (KTP Associate @ SBD Apparel) Academic Tutor in Cyber Security Academic Tutor in Computer Science and Software Engineering Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Research Associate (AI-Enhanced Predictive Modelling and Optimisation) Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Electrical and Electronic Engineering Research Associate/Senior Research Associate in Control for Soft Robot Wearable Assistance Research Associate Lecturer in Renewable Energy and Life Cycle Sustainability Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email 